{title: 466 - Wonderful Peace}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #466 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 466}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Far away in the depths [Em]of my [G]spirit tonight,
[G]Rolls a melody sweeter than psalm;
[Em]In celestial [C/G]like strains [G]it unceasingly [F#dim]falls
[G]O’er my soul like an infinite calm.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Em]Peace! Peace! [G]wonderful peace,
[G/B]Coming [F#m/C#]down [D]from [G]the [Bm]Father [G]above;
[Em]Sweep over [C/G]my spirit [G]forever, I [Am/C]pray,
[G]In fathomless billows of love.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]What a treasure I have [Em]in this [G]wonderful peace,
[G]Buried deep in [F#dim]my inner [G]most soul,
[Em]So secure [C/G]that no power [G]can mine it [F#dim]away,
[G]While the years of eternity roll!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]I believe when I rise [Em]to that [G]city of peace,
[G]Where the Author [F#dim]of [G]peace I shall see,
[Em]That one [C/G]strain of the song [G]which the ransomed [F#dim]will sing,
[G]In that heavenly kingdom will be-
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Weary soul, without gladness [Em]or [G]comfort or rest,
[G]Passing down [F#dim]the rough [G]pathway of time!
[Em]Make the [C/G]Savior your friend [G]ere the shadows [F#dim]grow dark;
[G]O accept of this peace so sublime.
{end_of_verse}
